UID:10017373-1795003200-1795006800@www.mhainspire.org
SUMMARY:Youth Mental Health First Aid Training for ADULTS - November 2026
DESCRIPTION:Youth Mental Health First Aid is designed for adults who regularly interact with young people ages 12–18. It teaches parents\, caregivers\, family members\, teachers\, school staff\, and other caring adults how to recognize and respond to mental health or substance use challenges and support a young person who may be experiencing a crisis. \nThe Course will: \n\nIntroduce common mental health challenges for youth\nReview typical adolescent development\nTeach a 5-step action plan for how to help young people in both crisis and non-crisis situations\n\n\nParticipants will receive certification after completion of all pre and post work\, as well as 4 live virtual training sessions.\nRegistration closes 11/10.
URL:https://www.mhainspire.org/event/youth-mental-health-first-aid-training-for-adults-november-2026-2/2026-11-18/
LOCATION:Virtual
CATEGORIES:NJ4S
END:VEVENT
